# Compose reads this file automatically as ./.env. Copy it to .env and fill in
# a value; .env is gitignored, this file is not.

# The PostgreSQL superuser password, shared by the database, the engine's
# DATABASE_URL and the portal's DB_PASSWORD. Compose refuses to start if it is
# unset rather than falling back to a default, because a default committed here
# is a default every install would keep. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 24
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
